5 words
-1 ls  ( <dir> -- )
  context: ~os   source: lib/os/ls
  Lists the folder named by the rest of the line, or the current folder: the
  names sorted, folders ending in /, hidden names (.git) left out, in lines
  of up to 72 columns.  `ls /reva/lib` lists the built-in libraries.  Built in: the first use loads os/ls.
pp  ( <file> -- )
  context: ~highlight   source: lib/highlight/core
  Lists FILE in colour (plain when the output is not a terminal); a name
  that is not a file is looked up under lib/, so `pp turtle/fractals` lists
  that library.  Built in: the first use loads highlight/core.
